---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const questions = [
  ['Can every fact name its source?', '"I researched it" doesn’t count. Name the actual source. If a number can’t say where it came from, it’s an assumption wearing a suit.'],
  ['Does something check that source automatically, or only a human on a good day?', 'Humans skim, and experts skim faster. The check has to actually run every time, without anyone remembering to do it.'],
  ['When the check fails, does it block the document, or warn and get ignored?', 'In my experience, warnings get ignored by the third week. A failed check should stop the document from shipping until a person decides what to do.'],
  ['Could you show someone the receipt six months from now?', 'A record of every claim, its source, and whether it passed. When the VP asks where 62% came from, that’s what you want to hand them.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Trust Checklist"
  description="Four questions to ask before any AI output reaches a real decision. From Build an AI Analyst You Can Trust."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 mb-3">
      <a href="/trust/" class="hover:underline">Build an AI Analyst You Can Trust</a> · one-page checklist
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-serif mb-4">
      The Trust Checklist
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
      Four questions to ask before any AI output reaches a real decision. Ask them about your own work first.
    </p>

    <ol class="space-y-4 counter-reset list-none pl-0">
      {questions.map(([q, a], i) => (
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 p-5 flex gap-4">
          <span class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 tabular-nums leading-none shrink-0 w-8">{i + 1}</span>
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-lg text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-1">{q}</div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">{a}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-primary-500 bg-primary-50 dark:bg-primary-950/30 rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4">
      <b class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-semibold">If any answer is no</b>, you've built a demo that isn't
      ready to be a teammate yet. That's fine. Now you know which of the four to fix first.
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
      From <em>Build an AI Analyst You Can Trust</em>, BrainStation Toronto · Khaled Zaky
      · <a href="https://khaledzaky.com" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">khaledzaky.com</a>.
      Engineers would call this an eval, risk teams a guardrail, and regulators governance. It's the same four
      questions either way.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 print:hidden">
      If you want to turn these four questions into an engineering practice,
      read <a href="/trust/evals/" class="text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400 hover:underline">Evals in Real Life</a>.
      It covers the kinds of evals, when to trust a model to judge, and the ones I'd run on a real analyst.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3 print:hidden">
      <button type="button" id="print-btn" class="btn-solid">Print or save as PDF</button>
      <a class="btn-outline" href="/trust/">Back to the workshop</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .btn-solid { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--color-primary-600); color: #fff; padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; border: 0; cursor: pointer; }
  .btn-solid:hover { background: var(--color-primary-700); }
  .btn-outline { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-gray-300); padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-gray-900); text-decoration: none; }
  .btn-outline:hover { background: var(--color-gray-50); }
  .dark .btn-outline { border-color: var(--color-gray-700); color: #fff; }
  .dark .btn-outline:hover { background: var(--color-gray-900); }
  @media print {
    header, footer { display: none !important; }
    #print-btn { display: none !important; }
    li { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  var pb = document.getElementById('print-btn');
  if (pb) pb.addEventListener('click', function () { window.print(); });
</script>
